{
  "format": "fugaro mailbox schema bound vectors",
  "why": "The merged vectors.json pins the tag, the direction, and the refusals of values far past a bound. It happens to sit on TWO lengths, because every case carries a tag of exactly MAC_MAX (64) and every action case a head SHA of exactly SHA_MIN (40), and its replay therefore holds those two. Everything else a phone can press against is pinned by nothing: no case sits on a string bound, a list bound, a repository or run bound, the second head-SHA length, or the C0, DEL and carriage-return rules. A bound moved by one therefore survived on both ends \u2014 `> TARGET_MAX` -> `>= TARGET_MAX` refused a 200-code-unit repository in Go and in JavaScript with both suites green, and `> TARGET_MAX` -> `> TARGET_MAX + 1` accepted a 201-code-unit one. This file is that follow-up, and it adds only the rows the merged file does not already hold.",
  "contract": "Every row here is asserted by BOTH ends: the JavaScript parity test (shared/mailbox-schema/bounds.test.js) validates it with validateMessage/validateHeartbeat, and the Go binding replays it in internal/mailbox (TestTheSharedBoundVectorsHold) through Decode and its own validators. A row either end disagrees with fails on the side that is wrong, which is the property vectors.json has and the reason this file is shaped like it.",
  "past": "Every accepts row with a \"past\" entry is a BOUND row: the row is accepted, and the same row with one more code unit (or one more list entry) at \"at\" is refused with \"code\". That is what makes the row pin the bound exactly rather than approximately, and it is what tells a narrowed bound and a widened one apart on both ends. The rows without one are not about a bound \u2014 a carriage return in a body is a character rule \u2014 and two of the bound rows (the tag's length and a head SHA of SHA_MIN) are here for symmetry with the ends that were NOT held: a row a reader can compare against the merged file is worth more than a comment saying which rows the merged file happens to hold. An append row carries the entry it adds in \"add\", so the row tests the LIST bound and not the duplicate rule.",
  "not_vectors_json": "This is a NEW file; vectors.json is untouched. The reason is recorded where the replay lives (internal/mailbox/message_test.go, TestTheRefusalCodesNoRefusalVectorCarries): vectors.json is a merged P6.3 contract, the plan this work belongs to edits no merged module (\u00a713/\u00a714), and a consumer adding to it is a contract change under a consumer's review. A file neither end owns, that both ends consume, reaches the same end \u2014 both sides held by shared vectors \u2014 without changing the artifact P6.3 owns. The rows that belong in vectors.json proper are proposed there to P6.3's follow-up.",
  "record": "the record the value is judged as: \"message\" is validateMessage, \"heartbeat\" is validateHeartbeat",
  "accepts": [
